# Gate

Run this before claiming anything works. The style test fails the build.

 powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\format.ps1
 # Linux: clang-format -n --Werror --style=file $(git ls-files 'src/**/*.[ch]' 'src/**/*.cpp')
 python scripts\check.py .
 cmake --build --preset clang-release
 ctest --preset clang-release

| Rule | Requirement |
|---|---|
| 0 | Read the util catalog first. No `realloc` (use `re_strbuf` / `re_vec`). No `x &= x - 1` (use `re_bits`) |
| 1 | 500 lines per file. 60-line function bodies. Nesting <= 4 |
| 2 | 4-line banner. Folder <= 15 files under `src/` |
| 3 | Exactly one `#pragma once` per header |
| 4 | ASCII-only source bytes. `.md` is exempt |
| 5 | LF, one final newline, no trailing whitespace, no tabs |
| 6 | No `malloc` / `calloc` / `realloc` / `free` / `strdup` outside `src/utils`. Use `re_arena` |
| 7 | No `printf` / `puts` / `fprintf(stdout)` outside `re_jw*` / `re_text*` |
| 8 | No `strlen` / `strcmp` / `strcpy` / `strcat` / `sprintf` / `strtok` and kin. Use `re_str` / `re_strbuf`. `memcpy` / `memset` / `memcmp` on sized spans are fine |
| 9 | `re_` prefix (clang-tidy, advisory) |
| 10 | clang-format clean |

`tests/` is exempt from rules 7 and 8 only. `re_regex_priv.h` and `re_util.h` stay out of the aggregator and must still appear in the util catalog. `RE_VEC_PUSH` needs an lvalue; assign `f(x)` to a local first.

Every new header under `src/utils/` must appear in both `docs/util-catalog.md` and `src/utils/re_util.h`, except those two private headers.
